Only if they're at the same level of identification.  Case in point. 
Take 4 cancelled, but not identified, daggers (thus, uncursed and +0).
 Drop them on an altar.  Pick up your 4 uncursed daggers.  #name them
u+0.  The next time you find (or, in wizmode, wish for) a dagger that
is uncursed and +0, yet is only identified as 'a dagger', it will not
stack.  If you take this new dagger, drop it on an altar ('an uncursed
dagger'), then pick it up, it will stack with your other uncursed
daggers named u+0.

IOW, similarly identified objects (which can stack in the first place)
will stack in the same way, regardless of any #name you give them. 
'an uncursed dagger' will not stack with 'a dagger' even if both are
'an uncursed +0 dagger'.  I hope this makes sense to others!

